/T (These safe emails serve as a benchmark for identifying legitimate communications. .The 'Security alert' email, for instance, used calm, reassuring language \('If this was you, you don't need to do anything'\) rather than urgency. The Terms of Service update was purely informational and included a clear path to close the account if the user disagreed with the new terms. Both demonstrate what a legitimate, low-risk communication looks like: clean authentication, matching domains, and no manipulative language. Such communications reflect a healthy digital landscape where users can engage without fear of phishing attempts. Understanding the characteristics of safe emails is vital in developing a keen eye for identifying threats in one's inbox and fostering a more secure online environment.)
