/T (Common phishing indicators are critical for identifying suspicious emails. Look for mismatched sender addresses, which may not align with legitimate domains. Other indicators include mass-blast patterns, like Undisclosed Recipients, and urgency in language that creates fear. Emails that employ manipulative unsubscribe mechanisms or claim urgent action required, like account verification, are often phishing attempts. Recognizing these signs empowers users to remain vigilant against potential threats.)
/E (Common phishing indicators are critical for identifying suspicious emails. Look for mismatched sender addresses, which may not align with legitimate domains. Other indicators include mass-blast patterns, like Undisclosed Recipients, and urgency in language that creates fear. Emails that employ manipulative unsubscribe mechanisms or claim urgent action required, like account verification, are often phishing attempts. Recognizing these signs empowers users to remain vigilant against potential threats.)
