/T (Additional details on common indicators include: failing authentication checks such as SPF, DKIM, or DMARC, which are essential for verifying email legitimacy. Be cautious of vague service identities and overly formal language that can indicate deception. Links that redirect through suspicious domains or use tracking services should raise red flags. Lastly, be wary of unsolicited attachments that could contain malware. Understanding these details can significantly enhance your email security awareness.)
