/E (Always stay vigilant against urgency tactics; genuine organizations rarely demand immediate action via email. Don't assume a professional-looking email is automatically legitimate, as attackers often use polished designs to deceive their targets. If you feel something is off, trust your instincts. Implementing these simple yet effective prevention strategies can significantly reduce your risk of falling victim to phishing scams and enhance your overall email security posture.)
