352 0 obj
<<
/Title (This exercise demonstrates that phishing detection requires both technical header analysis and content-based judgment. Authentication checks are a necessary but not sufficient signal of legitimacy. A combination of domain verification, content review, and healthy skepticism toward urgency and unnamed services provides the strongest defense against phishing attempts.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 230 0 R
/Next 353 0 R
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Title (Understanding the intricacies of phishing attacks is essential for both individuals and organizations. By recognizing common tactics and indicators, users can become proactive in their defenses. Continuous training and awareness campaigns will empower users to spot potential threats and report them promptly, thus creating a safer digital environment for all.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 230 0 R
/Prev 352 0 R
>>
endobj
