414 0 obj
<<
/Title (Essential Practices for Email Safety)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 350 0 R
/First 467 0 R
/Last 468 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
415 0 obj
<<
/Title (To effectively combat phishing threats, it's crucial to avoid certain common pitfalls. Don't trust an email solely because it has passed SPF, DKIM, or DMARC checks; these can be manipulated by anyone using free platforms. Moreover, never click on links or open attachments from unexpected emails, even if they appear to come from familiar senders. Additionally, avoid replying to spam to unsubscribe unless you're certain the source is legitimate, as this can confirm your address is active and lead to more unsolicited emails.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 351 0 R
/Next 416 0 R
>>
endobj
416 0 obj
<<
/Title (Always stay vigilant against urgency tactics; genuine organizations rarely demand immediate action via email. Don't assume a professional-looking email is automatically legitimate, as attackers often use polished designs to deceive their targets. If you feel something is off, trust your instincts. Implementing these simple yet effective prevention strategies can significantly reduce your risk of falling victim to phishing scams and enhance your overall email security posture.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 351 0 R
/Prev 415 0 R
>>
endobj
