467 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Prevention and Awareness Guidelines are essential for recognizing and mitigating phishing threats. Always verify the sender's actual email domain instead of relying on the display name. Hovering over links before clicking allows you to see the real destination. It's crucial to check header authentication results such as SPF, DKIM, and DMARC using tools like Google Header Analyzer or MxToolbox when in doubt. If an email claims urgent action, contact the organization directly through a known official channel to confirm its authenticity.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 414 0 R
/Next 468 0 R
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Title (Additionally, reporting suspicious emails to your IT or security team enhances your organization's overall security posture. This proactive approach helps in identifying patterns of phishing attempts and can lead to more effective measures being put in place. Educating employees about these do's not only empowers them to be vigilant but also creates a culture of security awareness. Regular training sessions can reinforce these guidelines, ensuring that everyone understands the critical nature of email security and how to navigate potential threats.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 414 0 R
/Prev 467 0 R
>>
endobj
