520 0 obj
<<
/Title (Common phishing indicators are critical for identifying suspicious emails. Look for mismatched sender addresses, which may not align with legitimate domains. Other indicators include mass-blast patterns, like Undisclosed Recipients, and urgency in language that creates fear. Emails that employ manipulative unsubscribe mechanisms or claim urgent action required, like account verification, are often phishing attempts. Recognizing these signs empowers users to remain vigilant against potential threats.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 466 0 R
/Next 521 0 R
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Title (Additional details on common indicators include: failing authentication checks such as SPF, DKIM, or DMARC, which are essential for verifying email legitimacy. Be cautious of vague service identities and overly formal language that can indicate deception. Links that redirect through suspicious domains or use tracking services should raise red flags. Lastly, be wary of unsolicited attachments that could contain malware. Understanding these details can significantly enhance your email security awareness.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 466 0 R
/Prev 520 0 R
>>
endobj
